Apple Touch ID: accept /dev/sep-bio interface version 5 as well as 4.

The aurora kernel moved /dev/sep-bio to interface version 5 (aurora-silicon/linux
f70f1acd35, "soc: apple: guard SEP enrolment and recover exact identities"): the
enrolment request grew from 136 to 144 bytes (account_uid, finger), so its ioctl
number changed, and a new SEP_BIO_PREPARE_ENROL must run before the first
enrolment. GET_INFO, LIST, VERIFY_START/POLL, CANCEL, DELETE and ATTEST keep the
version 4 layout. With version 4 hard-coded, fprintd ignores the reader on such a
kernel ("interface version 5, expected 4").

This is two patches from aurora-silicon/alarm-aurora packages/libfprint-aurora
(commit cc8d296f, "SEP: ship the v4/v5 userspace and guarded enrolment"; unchanged
in 2dbe4cd9), originally from aurora-silicon/aurora-sep-userspace b2bd710c:
  0004-aurora-refuse-unbound-enrollment.patch  (blob 3b8a40f3, sha256 55793f88...)
  0005-aurora-support-v4-and-v5.patch           (blob 87f412a7, sha256 8024015e...)
The only change in aurora.c is the rename to this driver's names (SEP_BIO_ to
AURORA_BIO_, struct sep_bio_ to struct aurora_bio_). After the rename both apply to
the driver as aurora-apple-sep.patch, aurora-touchid-retry.patch and
aurora-touchid-lid-switch.patch leave it, with no offset or fuzz. 0005 needs 0004:
its context is 0004's enrolment code. aurora-bio.h, which upstream takes from the
kernel's uapi header instead, gets the version 5 enrolment request and
AURORA_BIO_PREPARE_ENROL, copied from the kernel's include/uapi/linux/apple-sep.h.
The version 4 request stays private to aurora.c (aurora_enrol_start_v4), so
enrolment still works on a version 4 kernel.

